    "aboutTitle": "One map. Every pair.",
    "aboutBody": "<p>Choose a weekday or weekend and a time in Beijing, or play through the day. Geography shows physical positions. Travel time smoothly bends the city to represent estimated journey times among all 21 landmarks. Choosing a pair or searching for a route never changes the overall map shape.</p><h3>Traffic and travel times</h3><p>Local traffic assumptions cover commuting, tourism, shopping, evening activity, station approaches and persistent inner-city bottlenecks. Each road has a time multiplier based on its location, road class and selected time. Higher multipliers mean slower travel. These are illustrative assumptions, not measured or live traffic. Weather, holidays, incidents and unusual events are not included.</p><p>Road journeys are recalculated for half-hour snapshots. Each journey holds conditions fixed at its selected time. The map fits all 210 pairwise average times together; not all distances can fit exactly in two dimensions, so layout mismatch is shown. Roads, parks, water and landmarks share the same animated deformation. The camera stays fixed during playback.</p><h3>Search and routes</h3><p>Search the local map names and select a suggested start and destination. The route follows directed network edges and includes approximate access connectors. Its ETA is directional. Search does not cover every address or all of Beijing inside the Sixth Ring. A dimmed route marked Updating belongs to the timestamp still shown in its panel, until the next result arrives.</p><h3>Transport assumptions</h3><p>Drive uses roads only, including one-way restrictions and four minutes trip overhead. Turn restrictions and some access rules are missing. Bus is a road-corridor approximation with slower speeds and ten minutes waiting/access; actual bus lines and timetables are not included. Cycling uses its own network and fixed speeds.</p><p>For Bus and Bike, Allow subway compares the full road journey with walking, rail and walking again. Rail uses modelled running times, five-minute transfers and eight minutes entry/wait/exit plus one minute during strong commute demand or three minutes otherwise. These are assumptions, not schedules. Rail lines between stations and endpoint connectors are schematic. Driving never uses subway.</p><p>Bus and subway estimates are only available within the conservative model window of 06:00–22:00. This does not claim that actual services stop then. Outside that window, Drive and Bike remain available.</p><h3>Data</h3><p>The map uses a September 2026 OpenStreetMap snapshot and uncalibrated traffic scenarios. It is an explanatory model, not live navigation. <a href=\"traffic.json\" download>Download traffic snapshots</a>.</p>",
